# Per-participant sequence pool (task/generate_sequences_pool.py output) --
# 800 small files (200 members x 2 tasks x .pkl/.json) is too much file-count
# churn for git to track usefully, and it's fully reproducible on demand via
# `python task/generate_sequences_pool.py --n_pool 200 --task both --seed 0`
# (the exact promoted parameters live in that script's own CLI defaults) --
# resolves the earlier open question about whether to commit this pool or
# consolidate it into fewer files: neither, just don't track it at all.
task/sequences_pool/

# Task sequence data files (superseded by task/sequences/*.pkl)
data/task_continuous.pkl
data/task_binary.pkl

